# A singular CD matrix (row 2 = row 1 / 2, exact in binary): no inverse
# exists. wcslib 8.10 ACCEPTS it: wcsset succeeds and wcsp2s computes every
# point (only wcss2p has no answer). We refuse it in transform.New
# (rule 7: sky->pixel would be undefined for every point).
# EXPECT-GO-ERROR: linear transform is singular
NOTE stricter: singular_cd
GRID 1 512 3 1 512 3
HEADER
NAXIS   = 2
NAXIS1  = 512
NAXIS2  = 512
CRVAL1  = 180.0
CRVAL2  = 30.0
CRPIX1  = 256.5
CRPIX2  = 256.5
CD1_1   = 0.0009765625
CD1_2   = 0.001953125
CD2_1   = 0.00048828125
CD2_2   = 0.0009765625
CTYPE1  = 'RA---TAN'
CTYPE2  = 'DEC--TAN'
